# Local runtime data (users.json fallback, etc.).
# Anchored with a leading slash so it matches only the repo-root directory.
# An unanchored `data/` also matches src/data/, which holds application source.
# Git kept tracking those files (ignore rules do not apply to tracked paths), but
# `gcloud builds submit` derives .gcloudignore from .gitignore without consulting
# the index, so src/data/* was silently dropped from the build context and the
# container build failed on `Could not resolve "./data/departments.js"`.
/data/

